Terminal output shown in the demo video (assets: two real runs recorded with asciinema, separate from the proof runs).
Both ran against Pharos mainnet via the hosted Chain MCP and the Docs MCP; the command is typed on screen.

=== documented

Pharos mainnet (chain 1672), every read pinned to block 20535003

[1/1] USDC (Circle-deployed) · decimals()
  contract 0xC879C018dB60520F4355C26eD1a6D572cdAC1815  (this address is listed on the docs Token Registry page)
  1. Docs MCP (askQuestion):
     "decimals() is a read-only token contract call that returns the number of decimal places used to display token amounts."
     "For USDC, Pharos examples use 6 decimals: the returned value 6 means divide raw token units by 10⁶ to get USDC."
     "* 1_000_000 raw units = 1 USDC * 10_000 raw units = 0.01 USDC So decimals() returns the precision count, not a balance or token amount."
     (checked: decimals() is named on https://docs.pharos.xyz/developer-guide/x402/x402-pacific-mainnet, https://docs.pharos.xyz/developer-guide/x402/x402-atlantic-testnet)
     sources:
       - Token Registry: https://docs.pharos.xyz/getting-started/token-registry
       - Circle CCTP: https://docs.pharos.xyz/tooling-and-infrastructure/cross-chain/circle-cctp
       - About Pharos: https://docs.pharos.xyz/introduction/readme
       - x402 Pacific Mainnet: https://docs.pharos.xyz/developer-guide/x402/x402-pacific-mainnet
  2. Chain MCP (eth_call @ 20535003): 6
  3. Reading: Docs: "decimals() is a read-only token contract call that returns the number of decimal places used to display token amounts. For USDC, Pharos examples use 6 decimals: the returned value 6 means divide raw token units by 10⁶ to get USDC. * 1_000_000 raw units = 1 USDC * 10_000 raw units = 0.01 USDC So decimals() returns the precision count, not a balance or token amount." The chain returned 6, so 1 whole token is 10^6 base units, and an amount shown with 6 decimal places is the base-unit integer divided by that.

via https://mcp.pharos.xyz/mcp (Chain MCP) and https://docs.pharos.xyz/~gitbook/mcp (Docs MCP)

